    "check": "the nine members the minute lists as duly elected, read from the photographed page; the votes and any unsuccessful candidates are not in the minute book"
  },
  "partyLabels": "none-recorded",
  "note": "Proportional representation (single transferable vote) under the Local Government (Ireland) Act 1919; polled 15 January 1920. The nine commissioners were elected together; the returning officer was William Manwell. At the first meeting, on 30 January 1920, T. C. Rogers J.P. was re-elected chairman and the members present signed the declaration. The votes are not yet found in the sources searched."
